    entry
      definitions
        entry
          definition "A support structure comprising joined parts or conglomerated particles and intervening open spaces of similar or larger size."
        entry
          definition "The arrangement of support beams that represent a building's general shape and size."
        entry
          definition "The larger branches of a tree that determine its shape."
        entry
          definition "A basic conceptual structure."
          example "These ‘three principles of connexion’ compose the framework of principles in Hume's account of the association of ideas."
        entry
          definition "A reusable piece of code (and, sometimes, other utilities) providing a standard environment within which an application can be implemented."
        entry
          definition "The identification and categorisation of processes or steps that constitute a complex task or mindset in order to render explicit the tacit and implicit."
